# Package documentation tone

Docstrings, README, and module comments describe **what the package is and how it works**.

## Do

- State purpose, types, functions, contracts, and usage.
- Name sibling packages only when the API relationship matters (e.g. "orthogonal to execution tags in ComputationalBackends").

## Do not

- Mention GitHub usernames, org names, or phrases like "jbphyswx ecosystem", "our package family", "the X suite".
- Paste chat/plan language into package records ("remediation", "mega-primary", "hub package").
- Market the repository or author in technical docs (copyright in LICENSE is fine).

If a sentence still makes sense after deleting every proper noun that is not a package/library name, keep it; otherwise rewrite.
